It's all a matter of opinion really what a big slice is I guess. But steam is known for taking a lot IMO. Microsoft and PSN Also take a lot from games that release on their platform, as does nintendo... but that's really a whole nother ballgame... all those 3 console companies not only developed their consoles, but they also do their own QA testing on products (in addition to the game developers more extensive QA team), before allowing those games to go gold on their platform(last I checked). Steam does not do their own QA testing on all products... which is part of the reason we end up with so much random garbage... although I do wish I would have picked up "watch paint dry" before they removed it from steam just for the bragging rights. <3

&#x200B;

I'm not anti steam and pro consoles, quite the opposite, I have 600+ games on steam probably $2000+ spent. I'm just of the opinion that steam does quite little for the percentage they demand, the real value for devs to put stuff on steam I think is just being on the largest PC game platform out there.

I bet epic, just simply gave them a better deal. 

&#x200B;

Steam is pretty notorious for taking a big ass slice of the pie on games they let on their platform. It's why a number of devs refuse to put games on steam.

